{"parentUuid":"6137ee0d-a241-496d-92ed-38a5fe498166","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"0cb0ffaf-0ce7-4ac2-82c7-317b2c960d87","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"squishy-yawning-papert","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_015dN8NDsRCx64MUcKHngc2B","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Google cluster data 2011 task_events schema CSV format columns\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"cluster-data/ClusterData2011_2.md at master · google/cluster-data\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/cluster-data/blob/master/ClusterData2011_2.md\"},{\"title\":\"Analysis and Clustering of Workload in Google\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1501.01426\"},{\"title\":\"First Steps Exploring the Google Cluster dataset with iPython | Mark Stillwell\",\"url\":\"https://stillwell.me/~mark/post/first-steps-exploring-the-google-cluster-dataset-with-ipython/\"},{\"title\":\"Google Cluster Trace Dataset Overview\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/google-cluster-trace-dataset\"},{\"title\":\"Google cluster-usage traces: format + schema Charles Reiss, John Wilkes\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Auday-Al-Dulaimy/post/Are-there-any-datasets-for-cloudSim/attachment/59d61de379197b807797be3e/AS:273823268573184@1442295962733/download/Google+cluster+usage+traces.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Google cluster-usage traces: format + schema\",\"url\":\"https://t1.daumcdn.net/cfile/tistory/26542633597592552C\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - google/cluster-data: Borg cluster traces from Google\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/google/cluster-data\"},{\"title\":\"Analyzing Traces from a Google Data Center\",\"url\":\"https://hal.science/hal-01870216/file/analyzing-traces-google.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Google Cluster Usage Traces | PDF | Computer Data Storage | Scheduling (Computing)\",\"url\":\"https://www.scribd.com/document/901116490/Google-Cluster-Usage-Traces\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Analysis and Clustering of Workload in Google Cluster Trace based on Resource Usage\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/270593953_Analysis_and_Clustering_of_Workload_in_Google_Cluster_Trace_based_on_Resource_Usage\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's information about the Google Cluster Data 2011 task_events schema CSV format columns:\n\n## Google Cluster Data 2011 - Task Events Schema\n\nThe task events table contains information about various events pertaining to different tasks and has thirteen columns which include fields such as timestamp, missing information, index of tasks, event type, and priority of a task which can be free priorities or a production priority.\n\n### Column Names\n\nThe task_events CSV columns are:\n1. `time`\n2. `missing`\n3. `job_id`\n4. `task_idx`\n5. `machine_id`\n6. `event_type`\n7. `user`\n8. `sched_cls`\n9. `priority`\n10. `cpu_requested`\n11. `mem_requested`\n12. `disk`\n13. `restriction`\n\n### Additional Details\n\n- The machineID, if present, indicates the machine onto which the task was scheduled. Each task has a priority, a small integer that is mapped here into a sorted set of values, with 0 as the lowest priority (least important). Tasks with larger priority numbers generally get preference for resources over tasks with smaller priority numbers.\n\n- Priorities in this trace range from 0 to 11 inclusive; bigger numbers mean \"more important\". 0 and 1 are \"free\" priorities; 9, 10, and 11 are \"production\" priorities; and 12 is a \"monitoring\" priority.\n\n- The scheduling class of a job indicates the latency sensitivity of this job, where 0 denotes a non-production task and 3 a latency-sensitive task.\n\n### Event Types\n\nThe event types include:\n- SUBMIT (0): A task or job became eligible for scheduling\n- SCHEDULE (1): A job or task was scheduled on a machine\n- FINISH (4): A task or job completed normally(no content)Records without missing data have no value (empty string) in the \"missing info\" field.\n\n### File Format\n\nEach dataset is packaged as a set of one or more files, each provided in a compressed CSV format.(no content)The trace directory includes sub-directories populated by CSV files with names like `part-XXXXX-of-YYYYY.csv.gz`, which should be considered part of a continuous data stream.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"3f485a9b-bde1-458a-8b14-9a4ff165256d","timestamp":"2026-01-29T05:51:16.935Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Google cluster data 2011 task_events schema CSV format columns","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_vrtx_01XRakQTF2CK5hyhHTGP2AAS","content":[{"title":"cluster-data/ClusterData2011_2.md at master · google/cluster-data","url":"https://github.com/google/cluster-data/blob/master/ClusterData2011_2.md"},{"title":"Analysis and Clustering of Workload in Google","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1501.01426"},{"title":"First Steps Exploring the Google Cluster dataset with iPython | Mark Stillwell","url":"https://stillwell.me/~mark/post/first-steps-exploring-the-google-cluster-dataset-with-ipython/"},{"title":"Google Cluster Trace Dataset Overview","url":"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/google-cluster-trace-dataset"},{"title":"Google cluster-usage traces: format + schema Charles Reiss, John Wilkes","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Auday-Al-Dulaimy/post/Are-there-any-datasets-for-cloudSim/attachment/59d61de379197b807797be3e/AS:273823268573184@1442295962733/download/Google+cluster+usage+traces.pdf"},{"title":"Google cluster-usage traces: format + schema","url":"https://t1.daumcdn.net/cfile/tistory/26542633597592552C"},{"title":"GitHub - google/cluster-data: Borg cluster traces from Google","url":"https://github.com/google/cluster-data"},{"title":"Analyzing Traces from a Google Data Center","url":"https://hal.science/hal-01870216/file/analyzing-traces-google.pdf"},{"title":"Google Cluster Usage Traces | PDF | Computer Data Storage | Scheduling (Computing)","