{"parentUuid":"3cb939de-d17a-445a-95dd-855d907a88ee","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"0cb0ffaf-0ce7-4ac2-82c7-317b2c960d87","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"squishy-yawning-papert","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_vrtx_01MjTNBSrPofg6tagCnpAcAz","type":"tool_result","content":"# Google Cluster Dataset Schema\n\n## Task Events Table\nAccording to the documentation and schema.csv file, task_events contains these fields:\n\n**Columns:** `'time', 'missing info', 'job ID', 'task index', 'machine_id', 'event type', 'user', 'scheduling class', 'priority', 'cpu request', 'memory request', 'disk space request', 'different machines restriction'`\n\n**Event Types:**\n- 0: SUBMIT\n- 1: SCHEDULE  \n- 2: EVICT\n- 3: FAIL\n- 4: FINISH\n- 5: KILL\n- 6: LOST\n- 7: UPDATE\n- 8: (implied as another valid type in the code)\n\nThe author notes that \"the 'time', 'event type', 'cpu request', and 'memory request'\" fields are most important for analysis.\n\n## Machine Events Table\n**Columns:** `'time', 'machine ID', 'event type', 'platform ID', 'cpu capacity', 'memory capacity'`\n\n**Event Types:**\n- 0: ADDED\n- 1: REMOVED\n- 2: UPDATED\n\n## Key Insight\nThe code tracks task state by monitoring events: \"if event type in [0, 7, 8]\" the task is added/updated, while \"event type in [2, 3, 4, 5, 6]\" indicates task removal."}]},"uuid":"4d494b73-4ee7-4d8f-af87-44b1ef7067cd","timestamp":"2026-01-29T05:51:59.815Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":375277,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Google Cluster Dataset Schema\n\n## Task Events Table\nAccording to the documentation and schema.csv file, task_events contains these fields:\n\n**Columns:** `'time', 'missing info', 'job ID', 'task index', 'machine_id', 'event type', 'user', 'scheduling class', 'priority', 'cpu request', 'memory request', 'disk space request', 'different machines restriction'`\n\n**Event Types:**\n- 0: SUBMIT\n- 1: SCHEDULE  \n- 2: EVICT\n- 3: FAIL\n- 4: FINISH\n- 5: KILL\n- 6: LOST\n- 7: UPDATE\n- 8: (implied as another valid type in the code)\n\nThe author notes that \"the 'time', 'event type', 'cpu request', and 'memory request'\" fields are most important for analysis.\n\n## Machine Events Table\n**Columns:** `'time', 'machine ID', 'event type', 'platform ID', 'cpu capacity', 'memory capacity'`\n\n**Event Types:**\n- 0: ADDED\n- 1: REMOVED\n- 2: UPDATED\n\n## Key Insight\nThe code tracks task state by monitoring events: \"if event type in [0, 7, 8]\" the task is added/updated, while \"event type in [2, 3, 4, 5, 6]\" indicates task removal.","durationMs":5391,"url":"https://stillwell.me/~mark/post/first-steps-exploring-the-google-cluster-dataset-with-ipython/"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3cb939de-d17a-445a-95dd-855d907a88ee"}
