ons can span long time periods and we need to wait for the job to finish, the timing-based join is unreliable.\n\nA better approach: Use a RichCoFlatMapFunction with a different strategy:\n- Store all session counts from stream 1\n- When job finishes from stream 2, compute max and emit\n\nBut we still have a timing problem - sessions might arrive after job finish event.\n\nFor bounded inputs (files), we can rely on the fact that when all records are processed, the watermark will reach MAX_VALUE and all windows will fire. The job finish event typically happens after all task events.\n\nLet me try a different approach using GlobalWindows with an end-of-window trigger:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":13,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5676,"cache_read_input_tokens":70218,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":5676,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1}},"requestId":"req_vrtx_011CXb9hfQquqZE98a8E4Tz1","type":"assistant","uuid":"009b9612-0f31-4355-852b-b41c5bedbe7a","timestamp":"2026-01-29T05:54:17.027Z"}
{"parentUuid":"009b9612-0f31-4355-852b-b41c5bedbe7a","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/app/workspace","sessionId":"0cb0ffaf-0ce7-4ac2-82c7-317b2c960d87","version":"2.1.19","gitBranch":"","slug":"squishy-yawning-papert","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-5-20251101","id":"msg_vrtx_017yuuJNK1835Wz5esHqEXQ3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_vrtx_01Fv49QWqebouXZyvqkg9ta3","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/app/workspace/src/main/java/clusterdata/query/LongestSessionPerJob.java","content":"package clusterdata.query;\n\nimport clusterdata.datatypes.JobEvent;\nimport clusterdata.datatypes.TaskEvent;\nimport clusterdata.utils.AppBase;\nimport org.apache.flink.api.common.eventtime.WatermarkStrategy;\nimport org.apache.flink.api.common.functions.AggregateFunction;\nimport org.apache.flink.api.common.functions.MapFunction;\nimport org.apache.flink.api.common.state.ListState;\nimport org.apache.flink.api.common.state.ListStateDescriptor;\nimport org.apache.flink.api.common.state.ValueState;\nimport org.apache.flink.api.common.state.ValueStateDescriptor;\nimport org.apache.flink.api.common.typeinfo.Types;\nimport org.apache.flink.api.java.tuple.Tuple2;\nimport org.apache.flink.api.java.utils.ParameterTool;\nimport org.apache.flink.configuration.Configuration;\nimport org.apache.flink.core.fs.FileSystem;\nimport org.apache.flink.streaming.api.datastream.DataStream;\nimport org.apache.flink.streaming.api.environment.StreamExecutionEnvironment;\nimport org.apache.flink.streaming.api.functions.KeyedProcessFunction;\nimport org.apache.flink.streaming.api.functions.co.KeyedCoProcessFunction;\nimport org.apache.flink.streaming.api.functions.windowing.ProcessWindowFunction;\nimport org.apache.flink.streaming.api.windowing.assigners.EventTimeSessionWindows;\nimport org.apache.flink.streaming.api.windowing.time.Time;\nimport org.apache.flink.streaming.api.windowing.windows.TimeWindow;\nimport org.apache.flink.util.Collector;\n\nimport java.time.Duration;\nimport java.util.ArrayList;\nimport java.util.List;\n\npublic class LongestSessionPerJob extends AppBase {\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {\n\n        ParameterTool params = ParameterTool.fromArgs(args);\n        String taskInput = params.get(\"task_input\", null);\n        String jobInput = params.get(\"job_input\", null);\n        String outputPath = params.get(\"output\", null);\n        System.out.println(\"task_input  \" + taskInput);\n        System.out.println(\"job_input  \" + jobInput);\n\n        // set up streaming execution environment\n        StreamExecutionEnvironment env = StreamExecutionEnvironment.getExecutionEnvironment();\n\n        // Read task events stream - filter only SUBMIT events\n        DataStream<TaskEvent> taskEvents = env\n                .readTextFile(taskInput)\n                .map(new MapFunction<String, TaskEvent>() {\n                    @Override\n                    public TaskEvent map(String line) throws Exception {\n                        return TaskEvent.fromString(line);\n                    }\n                })\n                .filter(event -> event != null && event.getEventType() == TaskEvent.SUBMIT)\n                .assignTimestampsAndWatermarks(\n                        WatermarkStrategy.<TaskEvent>forBoundedOutOfOrderness(Duration.ofMinutes(5))\n                                .withTimestampAssigner((event, ts) -> event.getTimestamp() / 1000) // Convert microseconds to milliseconds\n                );\n\n        // Read job events stream - filter finished jobs\n        DataStream<JobEvent> finishedJobs = env\n                .readTextFile(jobInput)\n                .map(new MapFunction<String, JobEvent>() {\n                    @Override\n                    public JobEvent map(String line) throws Exception {\n                        return JobEvent.fromString(line);\n                    }\n                })\n                .filter(event -> event != null && event.isFinished())\n                .assignTimestampsAndWatermarks(\n                        WatermarkStrategy.<JobEvent>forBoundedOutOfOrderness(Duration.ofMinutes(5))\n                                .withTimestampAssigner((event, ts) -> event.getTimestamp() / 1000) // Convert microseconds to milliseconds\n                );\n\n        // Session window on task submit events per job, counting tasks per session\n        // Session gap is 10 minutes (600 seconds = 600,000 ms)\n        // Output: (jobId, taskCount)\n        DataStream<Tuple2<Long, Long>> sessionCounts = taskEvents\n                .keyBy(TaskEvent::getJobId)\n                .window(EventTimeSessionWindows.withGap(Time.minutes(10)))\n                .aggregate(new CountAggregate(), new SessionWindowFunction());\n\n        // Convert finished jobs to (jobId, finished=true)\n        DataStream<Tuple2<Long, Boolean>> finishedJobMarkers = finishedJobs\n                .map(new MapFunction<JobEvent, Tuple2<Long, Boolean>>() {\n                    @Override\n                    public Tuple2<Long, Boolean> map(JobEvent event) throws Exception {\n                        return Tuple2.of(event.getJobId(), true);\n                    }\n                })\n                .keyBy(t -> t.f0)\n                .process(new DeduplicateFinishedJobs());\n\n        // Join session counts with finished job markers using KeyedCoProcessFunction\n        // Buffer session counts and emit max when job finish arrives\n        DataStream<Tuple2<Long, Long>> result = sessionCounts\n                .keyBy(t -> t.f0)\n                .connect(finishedJobMarkers.keyBy(t -> t.f0))\n                .process(new MaxSessionForFinishedJobs());\n\n        // Write output\n        result.map(new MapFunction<Tuple2<Long, Long>, String>() {\n                    @Override\n                    public String map(Tuple2<Long, Long> value) throws Exception {\n                        return \"(\" + value.f0 + \",\" + value.f1 + \")\";\n                    }\n                })\n                .writeAsText(outputPath, FileSystem.WriteMode.OVERWRITE)\n                .setParallelism(1);\n\n        env.execute(\"LongestSessionPerJob\");\n    }\n\n    // Aggregate function to count tasks in a session\n    public static class CountAggregate implements AggregateFunction<TaskEvent, Long, Long> {\n        @Override\n        public Long createAccumulator() {\n            return 0L;\n        }\n\n        @Override\n        public Long add(TaskEvent value, Long accumulator) {\n            return accumulator + 1;\n        }\n\n        @Override\n        public Long getResult(Long accumulator) {\n            return accumulator;\n        }\n\n        @Override\n        public Long merge(Long a, Long b) {\n            return a + b;\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Window function to emit (jobId, taskCount)\n    public static class SessionWindowFunction\n            extends ProcessWindowFunction<Long, Tuple2<Long, Long>, Long, TimeWindow> {\n        @Override\n        public void process(Long jobId, Context context, Iterable<Long> elements,\n                            Collector<Tuple2<Long, Long>> out) {\n            Long count = elements.iterator().next();\n            out.collect(Tuple2.of(jobId, count));\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Deduplicate finished job events (take first occurrence)\n    public static class DeduplicateFinishedJobs\n            extends KeyedProcessFunction<Long, Tuple2<Long, Boolean>, Tuple2<Long, Boolean>> {\n\n        private ValueState<Boolean> seen;\n\n        @Override\n        public void open(Configuration parameters) {\n            seen = getRuntimeContext().getState(\n                    new ValueStateDescriptor<>(\"seen\", Types.BOOLEAN));\n        }\n\n        @Override\n        public void processElement(Tuple2<Long, Boolean> value, Context ctx,\n                                   Collector<Tuple2<Long, Boolean>> out) throws Exception {\n            if (seen.value() == null) {\n                seen.update(true);\n                out.collect(value);\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    // Process function to emit max session count for finished jobs\n    // Uses timer-based approach to ensure all session counts are received before emitting\n    public static class MaxSessionForFinishedJobs\n            extends KeyedCoProcessFunction<Long, Tuple2<Long, Long>, Tuple2<Long, Boolean>, Tuple2<Long, Long>> {\n\n        private ValueState<Long> maxSessionCount;\n        private ValueState<Long> jobFinishTime;\n        private ValueState<Boolean> hasEmitted;\n\n        // Timer delay: 10 minutes (session gap) + buffer to ensure all sessions are received\n        private static final long TIMER_DELAY_MS = 10 * 60 * 1000L + 5 * 60 * 1000L; // 15 minutes\n\n        @Override\n        public void open(Configuration parameters) {\n            maxSessionCount = getRuntimeContext().getState(\n                    new ValueStateDescriptor<>(\"maxSessionCount\", Types.LONG));\n            jobFinishTime = getRuntimeContext().getState(\n                    new ValueStateDescriptor<>(\"jobFinishTime\", Types.LONG));\n            hasEmitted = getRuntimeContext().getState(\n                    new ValueStateDescriptor<>(\"hasEmitted\", Types.BOOLEAN));\n        }\n\n        @Override\n        public void processElement1(Tuple2<Long, Long> sessionCount,\n                                    Context ctx,\n                                    Collector<Tuple2<Long, Long>> out) throws Exception {\n            // Update max session count\n            Long currentMax = maxSessionCount.value();\n            if (currentMax == null || sessionCount.f1 > currentMax) {\n                maxSessionCount.update(sessionCount.f1);\n            }\n        }\n\n        @Override\n        public void processElement2(Tuple2<Long, Boolean> finishedMarker,\n                                    Context ctx,\n                                    Collector<Tuple2<Long, Long>> out) throws Ex